# gdoc-meeting-summary

A Claude Code **skill** that reads a meeting transcript living in a Google Doc and
writes a clean, **bilingual (English + 繁體中文)** meeting summary into a **new tab**
of the same doc — leaving the original transcript untouched.

It works through the **Composio MCP gateway**, so no raw Google credentials are
needed; Composio holds the connected Google account.

## What it does
1. Reads the transcript from the Google Doc.
2. Generates a full bilingual summary (9 sections + a To-Do table and a
   Commitments table), neutral about identities, with uncertain values flagged
   `[待確認]`.
3. Creates a new tab and writes the summary into it.
4. Verifies the content landed in the new tab.

## Install (local)
Copy this folder to your skills directory:

```
~/.claude/skills/gdoc-meeting-summary/      # macOS/Linux
%USERPROFILE%\.claude\skills\gdoc-meeting-summary\   # Windows
```

Then connect Composio once (see `references/setup.md`):

```bash
claude mcp add --scope user --transport http composio https://connect.composio.dev/mcp \
  --header "x-consumer-api-key: <YOUR_COMPOSIO_CONSUMER_KEY>"
claude mcp list   # expect: composio … ✓ Connected
```

Make sure a **googledocs** connection is active in Composio (one-time OAuth).

## Use
In any session, just point Claude at a doc:

> Summarize https://docs.google.com/document/d/<DOC_ID>/edit into a new tab

The skill triggers automatically on requests like "summarize this transcript",
"create another tab and summarize it", or "整理這份逐字稿".

## Install (repo / team)
Commit this folder under your repo at `.claude/skills/gdoc-meeting-summary/` and a
`.mcp.json` at the repo root (template in `assets/mcp.json.example`). Provide the
Composio key via the `COMPOSIO_CONSUMER_KEY` environment variable — never commit
the key.

## Run automatically (CI / cron)
See `assets/github-action.example.yml` for a GitHub Actions workflow that runs the
skill headlessly with `claude -p`. Store the key as the repo secret
`COMPOSIO_CONSUMER_KEY`. The target Google account must already be connected in
Composio (do the OAuth once, ahead of time).

